sh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"09b7ee838dedc649d4017c2f5f043003476cecb8cda1a7a2a124dcea791f0949","event_uuid":"c5347c54-7eed-49f0-9229-2da52a94a638","position":{"commit_sha":"6194b9b485ae0383c2cacb7b356e4940611f8ae4","position":"1784944817009913001-c5347c54-7eed-49f0-9229-2da52a94a638"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"474a4700de02041f32bb597d95a075b6ffa22bcf1673536af4f565c138dbf443","event_uuid":"6b78b297-d4a5-431c-afb6-bd9379ba940a","position":{"commit_sha":"6c4e4dd3b03dd113a5e62d087a5be6f37ac17e71","position":"1784945891547546001-6b78b297-d4a5-431c-afb6-bd9379ba940a"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":"claude-code_2-1-219_agent","claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":"09e12a48-5d5d-4664-be59-0f39ae05a9e8","comments":[],"created_at":1784939070032303001,"creation_channel":"python","deps":[{"link_uuid":"686ad3e2-7d15-4897-99c9-a2fed91ba2cd","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"58f2-b6ed-363e-4608"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n`docs/plan-review-gate.md` and the `review_plan` docstring both state that a `bug`\nshort-circuits to a bare exempt PASS with `runner=exempt`. Probing on origin/main showed a\n`bug` actually returns `runner='pydantic_ai'`, `coverage.llm_ran=True`, and a signature.\n\n**Investigation result (2026-07-24): the CODE is correct; the DOCS are stale.**\n\n`workflow_ops.plan_review_precheck` (`src/rebar/llm/plan_review/workflow_ops.py:160-175`)\nshort-circuits ONLY `session_log` / `code_review` / `identity`. Its inline comment records the\ndeliberate change:\n\n    BUG REVIEW TIER (epic 6982 / R4): a bug no longer short-circuits to a bare exempt-PASS.\n    It gets a LIGHT ADVISORY review — DET floor + necessity probe (registry.BUG_TIER_CRITERIA)\n    — but is NEVER BLOCKED ... so a bug always PASSes.\n\n`tests/unit/test_bug_review_tier.py` already pins exactly this, asserting `runner != \"exempt\"`\nfor a bug. So bugs being reviewed is an intentional feature, not a missing short-circuit.\n\n**This ticket's original acceptance criteria were therefore wrong.** They asked to \"make\nexempt types short-circuit as documented\", which would have REVERTED epic 6982. They have been\nrewritten to the real defect: two stale statements in the documentation. Criteria are corrected\nrather than closed-against-stale, per the remedy documented in 4636-432a-1871-4d74.\n\nNote the two distinct exemption axes that made the original claim look right: a bug needs no\nsigned attestation to be CLAIMED (a CLI-side exemption in `rebar._commands.gates`, unchanged),\nwhich is separate from whether the plan-review gate REVIEWS it. Conflating them is the trap.\n\n## Expected Behavior\nThe documentation describes what the code does: `session_log` / `code_review` / `identity` are\ngate-exempt (`runner=exempt`, no review); a `bug` is reviewed under the bug tier and can be\ncoached but never blocked.\n\n## Scope\n- `docs/plan-review-gate.md`\n- `src/rebar/llm/plan_review/__init__.py` (the `review_plan` docstring)\n\nNo behavior change.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `docs/plan-review-gate.md` no longer claims bugs are exempt from the gate, and names\n      `session_log` / `code_review` / `identity` as the exempt types; verified by\n      `grep -q 'A \\*\\*bug is NOT' docs/plan-review-gate.md`.\n- [ ] The never-signed passage no longer lists `bug` as an exempt runner; verified by\n      `grep -q 'a\\n\\`bug\\` is reviewed under the bug tier' docs/plan-review-gate.md` or by\n      reading the section — it must say a bug is NOT exempt there.\n- [ ] The `review_plan` docstring describes the bug review tier instead of claiming bugs are\n      exempt; verified by\n      `grep -q 'bug review tier' src/rebar/llm/plan_review/__init__.py`.\n- [ ] The CLI claim-time bug exemption is called out as a separate axis, so the two are not\n      conflated again.\n- [ ] `tests/unit/test_bug_review_tier.py` still passes (no behavior change).\n- [ ] `make lint`, `make typecheck`, and the default non-integration pytest suite exit zero.\n","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[],"keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","managed_refs":[],"parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"0d93633c-2b1e-410e-bede-99336e3e8cc7","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"26a4-a0e8-e539-464d","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Docs wrongly claim bug tickets are gate-exempt (the bug review tier reviews them)","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["f0ed8bb7-32fb-4f81-867b-970c04507671","686ad3e2-7d15-4897-99c9-a2fed91ba2cd","0d93633c-2b1e-410e-bede-99336e3e8cc7","c5347c54-7eed-49f0-9229-2da52a94a638","6b78b297-d4a5-431c-afb6-bd9379ba940a"]},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1784945891547546002,"uuid":"ebfdfff3-9213-4710-8ebf-a9e276152427"}